zcode-tui is an unofficial, independent client. It is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or connected to Z.ai, and it contains no code from the ZCode
desktop or runtime: it spawns the locally installed, unmodified ZCode runtime
in protocol mode and speaks a documented wire protocol to it.

Runtime dependencies (npm, per package.json; licences verified
GPL-compatible at adoption — see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md):
  @opentui/core, @opentui/react          MIT   (Anomaly)
  react                                  MIT   (Meta / open source)
  typescript (devDependency)             Apache-2.0
  diff (transitive)                      BSD-3-Clause
  bun (runtime / build tool)             MIT   (Oven)

The bundled release binaries are produced by `bun build --compile`; the Bun
runtime is MIT-licensed. The corresponding source for every released binary
is this repository at the tagged commit.
